    "registration": {
      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "LI Wei 李蔚 (T. 景霱, 臺書, H. 坦園, 據梧居士), 1625–1684, July 22, official, was a native of Kao-yang, Chihli. An ancestor in the fifth generation, Li Yen 李儼 (T. 仲威, 1438–1503), was a chin-shih of 1478 who served as an assistant financial commissioner of Shansi.",
          "source": "eccp-3643665",
          "kind": "source-wording",
          "status": "imported"
        },
        {
          "text": "Li Wei 李衛 (T. 又玠, 1687?–1738, posthumous name 敏達). Unlike the first two, Li Wei was not a Bannerman. A native of Hsuchow, Kiangsu, he became a student in the Imperial Academy and purchased the rank of an assistant department director.",
          "source": "eccp-3656377",
          "kind": "source-wording",
          "status": "imported"
        }
      ]
    },
